# Band boundaries: Unicode CLDR 47 Day Period Rules, locale de
# (https://www.unicode.org/cldr/charts/47/supplemental/day_periods.html),
# transcribed in chronologia/dayparts.py as [05:00, 10:00).
# "früh" after a day word names that day's morning: DWDS, "früh",
# Bedeutung 2: "am Morgen, morgens" (https://www.dwds.de/wb/früh), as in
# "morgen früh" and "heute früh".  Bare "früh" is the adjective "early",
# so marker_daypart_after_day.voc limits it to the place after a day word.
# The noun "Morgen" is not here: it is also the word for tomorrow.
früh
